# Megabase CODEOWNERS
# 
# This file defines code ownership for the repository.
# Human maintainers own critical files that agents cannot modify without approval.
#
# See: https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners

# Human-owned files (per GOAL.md)
# These require human approval for any changes

/MANIFESTO.md           @AgenP/megabase-humans
/GOAL.md                @AgenP/megabase-humans
/HUMAN_LOG.md           @AgenP/megabase-humans

# Vendor directory - pinned upstream sources
# Humans own submodule version decisions
/vendor/                @AgenP/megabase-humans

# Judge directory - external correctness arbiter
# Changes require reviewer agent approval, then human merge
/judge/                 @AgenP/megabase-humans @AgenP/megabase-reviewer

# Security-sensitive files
/.github/workflows/     @AgenP/megabase-humans
/CODEOWNERS             @AgenP/megabase-humans

# Everything else can be modified by agents
# (but still requires PR review per branch protection rules)
